  "headline": "Stew and Kuhl Swap Backfields, Then Both Get Screwed",
  "publicationDraft": "Stew bought into Barkley’s ACL comeback as his workload recovered, while Kuhl acquired three backs with credible early-season opportunities. Barkley and Edwards-Helaire both suffered injuries on October 10, wrecking each manager’s principal acquisition. Drake and Ty'Son Williams had already been cut on October 6, and Hines never entered an observed Kuhl starting lineup before his November release. Both headline backs returned in Week 11. Edwards-Helaire outscored Barkley 25.70–24.40 in the paired Weeks 14–15, although the managers had different opponents. Neither side could predict the simultaneous injuries. Stew’s consolidation was defensible; Kuhl’s diversification looked better on paper than it did on his bench. Neither acquired the difference-maker he hoped for.",
